# Pentagonal sum elementary-symmetric identities (decomposition of the sextic resolvent)

This file decomposes the core polynomial identity behind `sexticResolvent_pentagonalSum_root`
(in `PentagonalSum.lean`) into the six elementary-symmetric coefficient identities of the
six pentagonal-sum-squares.

## Mathematical background

Let `v 0,...,v 4` be the roots of `X^5 + p X + q`, so the elementary symmetric functions
satisfy `e1 = e2 = e3 = 0`, `e4 = p`, `e5 = -q`.

There are exactly `[S5 : F20] = 6` left cosets of the Frobenius group `F20 = AGL(1,F5) ≤ S5`.
Representatives (all fixing `0` and `1`) are
  rep0=id, rep1=(3 4), rep2=(2 3), rep3=(2 3 4), rep4=(2 4 3)... ,
giving the six pentagonal sums `P0,...,P5` below (`Pj = pentagonalSum (v ∘ repj)`).
When `e2 = 0`, `F20` stabilises each `Pj^2`, so the six values `t_j := Pj^2` are exactly the
roots of the sextic resolvent `R6`.  Writing `R6 = ∏ (X - t_j)`, comparing coefficients gives:

  e1(t) = Σ t_j           = 10 p          (degree  4 in v)
  e2(t) = Σ_{i<j} t_i t_j = 55 p^2        (degree  8)
  e3(t) = Σ t_i t_j t_k   = 140 p^3       (degree 12)
  e4(t)                   = 175 p^4       (degree 16)
  e5(t)                   = 106 p^5 + 3125 q^4   (degree 20)
  e6(t) = ∏ t_j           = 25 p^6        (degree 24) -/

